id: pm-review-import
title: "Import every bot thread, review and issue comment idempotently"
description: ""
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-12T10:47:29.083Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-12T13:32:36.666Z"
author: codex-sol
acceptance_criteria: Paginate all connections and nested replies; stable GitHub node IDs; typed schema fields; commit links; preserve verdicts; informational noise classification; pm search visibility.
parent: pm-review-epic
release: 2026.10.12
comments[10]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-12T10:52:32.558Z",codex-sol,"SDK design: ReviewFinding type and namespaced typed fields are registered on activation and persisted through schema APIs during import. Complete-corpus reads include terminal items. Thread identity is the thread node, with all replies available to the transport; review and issue-comment identities remain distinct. Missing issue-comment commit provenance stays unknown rather than being guessed."
  "2026-10-12T11:23:54.616Z",codex-sol,"Behavioral revert proof for this new package: disabling prior-verdict preservation in importFindings makes node --test --test-name-pattern=\"real SDK upsert\" test/core.test.ts fail. Restoring the function returns the regression to green; real SDK comments and fields survive re-import."
  "2026-10-12T12:14:00.257Z",codex-sol,"Explicit finding/priority/severity markers now take precedence over noise words. An actionable rate-limit or walkthrough-generator finding stays pending; genuine unmarked quota/trial/failure/walkthrough notices remain informational. Removing this guard alone makes node --test --test-name-pattern=\"marker parsing\" test/core.test.ts fail. Correct behavior restored before full gates."
  "2026-10-12T12:25:42.054Z",codex-sol,"Resume audit found the final npm gate failing: word boundaries did not match CodeRabbit Markdown underscores in the actionable marker guard. Correcting delimiter handling, checking every actionable marker family, and rerunning the behavioral disable proof before both complete release gates."
  "2026-10-12T12:26:17.321Z",codex-sol,"Corrected Markdown delimiter handling and verified CodeRabbit, nitpick, Gemini priority and explicit severity markers retain actionable findings despite noise words. Focused test passes 1/1. Corrected revert proof: disabling only isInformational's actionable-marker guard makes that test fail 0/1 with true !== false; restoring the function passes 1/1. This supersedes the earlier guard receipt whose baseline failed the full npm gate."
  "2026-10-12T13:22:57.750Z",codex-sol,Review round 1 confirms outside-diff and nitpick review bodies are misclassified and two uncontrolled-input regexes backtrack polynomially. Verify title sanitization alert against actual plain-text sinks before deciding.
  "2026-10-12T13:30:23.688Z",codex-sol,"Finding 4248463280: outside-diff, nitpick-count, refactor and severity markers keep review bodies pending. node --test --test-name-pattern=\"review body sections\" test/core.test.ts passes against real temporary trackers; reverting only isInformational fails (exit 1)."
  "2026-10-12T13:30:24.693Z",codex-sol,"CodeQL 1 / 4248090349: priority separator regex now has disjoint delimiter/whitespace groups. node --test --test-name-pattern=\"severity parsing bounds\" test/core.test.ts passes with 150000 tabs; reverting only severityOf times out after 5000ms and fails (exit 1)."
  "2026-10-12T13:30:25.712Z",codex-sol,"CodeQL 2 / 4248090369: title markup and Markdown trims now use linear scanning. node --test --test-name-pattern=\"title parsing bounds\" test/core.test.ts passes with 150000 open brackets and spaces; reverting only summaryOf times out after 5000ms and fails (exit 1)."
  "2026-10-12T13:30:26.982Z",codex-sol,"CodeQL 3 / 4248090384: scanner removes complete, nested and truncated tag delimiters from summaries, with raw body preserved separately. node --test --test-name-pattern=\"title parsing removes\" test/core.test.ts passes; reverting only summaryOf fails on the truncated script tag (exit 1). No alert dismissed; plain-text storage does not establish an exploitable HTML sink."
